@*
    The one modal every create/edit form on a page is shown in (D42). It is deliberately empty:
    the button that opens it carries hx-get for the form partial and Bootstrap's own
    data-bs-toggle to show the modal, and the partial brings its own header, body and footer.

    site.js puts this placeholder back when the modal closes, so the next open never flashes the
    form that was in it last time.
*@
<div class="modal fade" id="form-modal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    @*
        Not modal-dialog-scrollable: the form sits between .modal-content and the header/body/
        footer, which is the wrong shape for that class's flex layout. A long form scrolls the
        page instead, which is what it did before.
    *@
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered modal-lg">
        <div class="modal-content" id="form-modal-content">
            <div class="modal-body">
                <p class="text-secondary mb-0">Loading…</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
